{% extends '@CitadelAureum/core/docs/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block article %}
    <p>
        Every employee account is created by a manager; there is no public
        signup. Creating an account, handing over credentials, and the
        employee's first login together take a couple of minutes.
    </p>

    <h2>Creating a new employee</h2>
    <ol class="au-docs-steps">
        <li>
            Open <strong>Manager → Staff</strong> and choose
            <strong>Create staff member</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
            Fill in their name, username, email, and timezone, then pick one or
            more roles. Roles decide which modules they can see and manage.
            You can only assign roles at or below your own level.
        </li>
        <li>
            Submit the form. Aureum generates a temporary password, emails a
            welcome message to the new employee, and shows you the credentials
            once. If the email fails to send, pass the credentials on securely
            yourself, because they are not shown again.
        </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="au-docs-note">
        <i class="ph ph-warning"></i>
        <p>
            If the username or email is already taken, the form will tell you.
            Check with other managers before retrying, as the person may already
            have an account.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>The employee's first login</h2>
    <ol class="au-docs-steps">
        <li>They sign in with the username and temporary password from the welcome email.</li>
        <li>
            Before anything else, Aureum requires them to set their own password:
            at least 12 characters, and not one that has appeared in a known data
            breach. The temporary password stops working immediately.
        </li>
        <li>They land on the dashboard with exactly the modules their roles allow.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Offboarding</h2>
    <p>
        When someone leaves, open <strong>Manager → Staff</strong>, choose the
        employee, and use <strong>Offboard</strong>. You'll be asked to confirm
        before anything happens. Offboarding removes their access; records they
        created (bookings, fines, logs) stay attached to the hotel.
    </p>

    <div class="au-docs-note">
        <i class="ph ph-info"></i>
        <p>
            Need a new role first? Roles and their module permissions are covered
            in the Roles &amp; access chapter.
        </p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
